WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
A bare hill in South Africa.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.310
A small drum lies in the grass.

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.240
Above it, unfamiliar stars wheel slowly.

4
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:12.780
Drummer Hodge came here
fresh from his Wessex home.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:18.920
He never understood this land, or why
there rose "Strange stars amid the gloam."

6
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:24.160
Now he lies buried here, far from
home, under those foreign stars.

7
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.720
So does Hodge belong here now?

8
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:30.010
In this mission, you'll meet
Thomas Hardy and the Boer War,

9
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:35.260
which began in October 1899, and
learn what the name Hodge meant.

10
00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:39.020
You'll sound out words like
kopje, veldt and Karoo,

11
00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:42.040
as strange to us as the land was to him.

12
00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.830
And you'll trace how the
poem moves through time,

13
00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.580
in three stanzas.

14
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:50.150
Your mission: decide
whether Hodge belongs now.
